{"id":5902,"date":"2021-11-09T12:38:16","date_gmt":"2021-11-09T12:38:16","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?p=5902"},"modified":"2021-11-09T13:02:45","modified_gmt":"2021-11-09T13:02:45","slug":"boosting-studentspotential-in-entrepreneurship-and-industry","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/boosting-studentspotential-in-entrepreneurship-and-industry\/","title":{"rendered":"Boosting Students\u2019 Potential in Entrepreneurship and Industry"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>The\u00a0AIMS Ghana Entrepreneurship Week (E-Week) is celebrated annually and being a\u00a0week-long program,\u00a0this year it started on October 11 and ended on October 15\u00a02021. It\u00a0was an opportunity to introduce this year&#8217;s batch of students to basic principles in the workplace as well as entrepreneurial\u00a0techniques.\u00a0Activities during the\u00a0one-week\u00a0period focused on\u00a0Career Development, Design Thinking Methodologies\u00a0an\u00a0Industrial visit and\u00a0a\u00a0Community Fact-finding\u00a0mission.\u00a0\u00a0<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>During this period, the Regular Master\u2019s Students got to take a break from the rigours of abstract mathematics, learn about problem-solving and ideation as well as build work ethics and skills which would be relevant in industry. The E-Week program&nbsp;has&nbsp;indeed&nbsp;become a necessity due to the impact it has had on students over the past years.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Day 1: Career Development, Communications&nbsp;and&nbsp;Etiquette&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The students&nbsp;were taken&nbsp;through three critical topics; Career Development, Communication, and Etiquettes. The session was completely interactive&nbsp;with students engaging&nbsp;in discussions on&nbsp;various employability skills&nbsp;and career development,&nbsp;led by&nbsp;Ms.&nbsp;Sarah Osei, a&nbsp;Program Manager at&nbsp;the&nbsp;Centre. This session included planning and mapping out a strategy to grow in the profession&nbsp;one&nbsp;chooses. This&nbsp;enabled students&nbsp;to&nbsp;re-examine their career&nbsp;choices&nbsp;in order&nbsp;to set realistic goals.&nbsp;There was also a&nbsp;session on communications and etiquettes focused on the style and form of communication at the workplace. During the presentation, Sarah focused the talk on the do&#8217;s and don&#8217;ts when it comes to Meeting People, Telephone and Video Calls, Correspondence, Dining and General Work Etiquette.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-1 wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped\"><ul class=\"blocks-gallery-grid\"><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3162-1-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"5903\" data-link=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?attachment_id=5903\" class=\"wp-image-5903\" srcset=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3162-1-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3162-1-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3162-1-768x512.jpg 768w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3162-1-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3162-1-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3162-1-18x12.jpg 18w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure><\/li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3361-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"5904\" data-link=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?attachment_id=5904\" class=\"wp-image-5904\" srcset=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3361-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3361-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3361-768x512.jpg 768w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3361-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3361-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3361-18x12.jpg 18w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure><\/li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3198-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"5907\" data-full-url=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3198-scaled.jpg\" data-link=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?attachment_id=5907\" class=\"wp-image-5907\" srcset=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3198-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3198-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3198-768x512.jpg 768w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3198-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3198-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3198-18x12.jpg 18w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure><\/li><\/ul><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>DAY 2 \u2013&nbsp;3:&nbsp;Training Sessions with Design Thinking Ghana&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Design thinking is&nbsp;recognized&nbsp;as one of the most effective tools&nbsp;used for&nbsp;entrepreneurial strategizing&nbsp;purposes. In this regard, two&nbsp;days were&nbsp;allocated for this training&nbsp;session,&nbsp;facilitated by Design Thinking Ghana&nbsp;consisting of Mr.&nbsp;Bryan&nbsp;Achiampong&nbsp;and his team. It started with exposure to the&nbsp;&#8220;Power of Design Thinking in Exploring Entrepreneurship and Intrapreneurship in a Global Village&#8221;.&nbsp;The class was divided into eight groups. Each group&nbsp;was to critically examine the Sustainable&nbsp;Development&nbsp;Goals,&nbsp;identify a problem&nbsp;and provide business solutions.&nbsp;Students were trained on how to develop a &#8216;point of view&#8217;, which entails sampling an individual from the whole population facing the problem identified&nbsp;and addressing their specific needs.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The session continued on day 3 with students were finally&nbsp;reaching&nbsp;the final stage of the design thinking process, which&nbsp;centres&nbsp;on developing a &#8216;Business Model Canvas&#8217;&nbsp;being an&nbsp;accumulation&nbsp;of various stages of the design thinking process. This allowed students to give a&nbsp;concise summary of the&nbsp;business&nbsp;plan and&nbsp;how to execute it. Students were given some time to put their work together, and final presentations&nbsp;were&nbsp;delivered.&nbsp;With&nbsp;critique&nbsp;and commendation,&nbsp;students demonstrated a unique ability to come up with fantastic ideas within a short period. Closing the&nbsp;design thinking&nbsp;session,&nbsp;Ms&nbsp;Sarah Osei applauded the students for&nbsp;exhibiting&nbsp;amazing work&nbsp;which could be considered for further development&nbsp;they were able to come up with within the limited time and space.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-3 wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped\"><ul class=\"blocks-gallery-grid\"><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/11\/IMG_3781-min-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"5909\" data-link=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?attachment_id=5909\" class=\"wp-image-5909\" srcset=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/u